      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Wisdom isn't in waiting for the ink to run dry; it's in choosing the moment the pen stops moving. To know when the story is finished is to possess the ultimate control over your own meaning. It is not a failure of the story, but the final, most powerful act of authorship. You have earned the right to dictate the final punctuation mark.",
      "source": "target",
